.TH GAME-OF-LIFE 1 "October 2026" "Game of Life" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
game-of-life \- small, colorful Conway Life worlds for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B game-of-life
.RI [ command ] " [options]"
.br
.B game_of_life
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watch 810 classic Life patterns grow, move and interact. Mint births, blue
trails and golden colonies are drawn at 15 frames per second by default.
Single figures have room to develop. Scene durations follow their behavior.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B preview
Alternate random cells, a single known figure and a sparse mix. The default.
.TP
.BI figure " name"
Show one instance of the named figure.
.TP
.B mix
Scatter separated figures from the library.
.TP
.B random
Start with random cells.
.TP
.BI figures " [text]"
List the library, optionally filtering names and families.
.TP
.B wallpaper
Draw underneath applications in an X11 desktop.
.TP
.B screensaver
Wallpaper plus an interactive screensaver after 120 idle seconds.
.TP
.B doctor
Report the available display, fonts, wallpaper and idle capabilities.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are passed to game_of_life and may follow a command.
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Maximum frame rate, 1 to 60; default 15.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " N"
Cell size in pixels, 1 to 128; 0 chooses an economical grid automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-trail " N"
Trail length, 0 to 31 generations; default 18.
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds " N"
Fixed scene duration, 10 to 3600 seconds; 0 uses adaptive timing.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle " N"
Inactivity threshold for wallpaper presentation; 0 disables, 1 to 86400 enables.
Requires libXss and an X11 desktop. Mouse movement leaves the saver displayed
so that clicks can navigate; any key returns to the desktop.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " en|fr"
Caption language. The default follows LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, then LANG.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Fullscreen preview. Any key exits; mouse clicks navigate.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Reproduce the initial world at identical dimensions.
.TP
.BI \-\-display " DISPLAY"
Select an X server.
.TP
.BI \-\-window-id " ID"
Draw in an existing window. Its host manages input and lifetime.
.TP
.B \-root
Draw in XSCREENSAVER_WINDOW if provided, otherwise in the X11 root window.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-\-version
Print help or version/build capabilities without opening a display.
.SH CONTROLS
Left click advances. Right click replays the preceding scene from its beginning.
The last 64 scene seeds are retained. Space advances in windowed preview;
Escape or Q closes it. Any key dismisses the idle saver while keeping the
wallpaper alive. Host-managed windows, including XScreenSaver, keep their own
input handling.
.SH PLATFORMS
Linux and BSD X11 desktops can run wallpaper and idle modes. Desktop shells
may cover a wallpaper window. macOS with XQuartz, Wayland with Xwayland and
Windows with WSLg can run the windowed preview; they do not gain native
wallpaper, idle detection or session locking through this program.
.SH FILES
No user configuration is required. No networking is performed. Patterns are
compiled into the executable. Installing does not enable autostart or change
screen power settings. The idle saver is not a session lock.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
game-of-life figure pulsar
game-of-life figures gun
game-of-life mix --fps 10
game-of-life screensaver --idle 300
game-of-life doctor
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xscreensaver (1),
.BR xset (1)
.br
